  "reason": "Lockfile-only security updates: anyio 4.8.0->4.14.2 (critical TLS host-name spoofing, used by httpx for every outbound HTTPS call), langsmith 0.7.26->0.8.18 (transitive via langgraph; requires websockets 14.2->15.0.1), vitest 4.1.10->4.1.11 (dev only), and time 0.3.45->0.3.47 plus serde_with 3.17->3.21 in the Tauri app, which needs rust-version 1.85->1.88. Selected tests cover the websockets callers (Codex harness RPC, API websocket routes), langgraph orchestration, httpx provider and MCP paths, and native modules that use time, cookies or Tauri config.",
  "exclusions": "No full suites. Three tests fail on main locally with both old and new dependency versions and are excluded by node id: test_harness_adapters.py::test_claude_native_capabilities_exclude_project_files_and_shell and two test_orchestration.py mission compaction tests. No Playwright: no UI code changed.",
